Cycle fake occlusion query sample counts (port of xenia-canary b447699a5)

A constant fake count makes Dishonored (425307E3) hide most meshes; Canary
counts down from upper to lower threshold (100..80) and starts over.

diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h
index da8e4324..a60073f1 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h
@@ -195,6 +195,10 @@ class CommandProcessor {
                                           uint32_t count);
   virtual bool ExecutePacketType3_EVENT_WRITE_ZPD(memory::RingBuffer* reader, uint32_t packet,
                                                   uint32_t count);
+  // Fake passed-sample count for the next finished occlusion query (Canary b447699a5):
+  // counts down from the upper to the lower threshold, then starts over, so consecutive
+  // results differ. Returns -1 when no count should be written.
+  static int64_t NextFakeOcclusionSampleCount();
   bool ExecutePacketType3Draw(memory::RingBuffer* reader, uint32_t packet, const char* opcode_name,
                               uint32_t viz_query_condition, uint32_t count_remaining);
   bool ExecutePacketType3_DRAW_INDX(memory::RingBuffer* reader, uint32_t packet, uint32_t count);
